KZ2 patch 7022: computed hops whose target is a link register plus a constant get a lift-time guess
(KZ3 patch 1098's SPU_IB_HOP_G), switched by KZ2_SPU_PCGUESS=1 (off by default until a heavy-view A/B).
The SPU job libraries open and close their interrupt windows with `brsl $r2, .+4 ; ai $r2, $r2, 8 ; bid|bie $r2` (and
`bihz $rC, $r2`): a computed hop to the instruction after the branch. compute_ib_guesses followed only `il`/`ila`
constants, so each of these hops went through spu_ib_direct (its state tests, the lookup memo and probe) and, with an
interrupt pending, the full resolver: Gfx.Particles.UpdateJob has 24 such sites around its lock-line helpers
(0xF6A0-0xFE20), VertexJob 11, Skinning 7; dispatch (spu_indirect_branch, spu_lifted_lookup, do_linear_probe_nonempty,
spu_ib_direct) was 14 % of UpdateJob's samples and 10 % of VertexJob's in the spu 35 profile (150-170 s).
Here resolve() also takes `brsl rX` (rX = its address + 4) and `ai rX, rY, K` (offset K) when the caller asks for
link-register guesses (pc_guesses); those (site, target) pairs are emitted as SPU_IB_GUESS_PC, which is SPU_IB_GUESS
behind g_kz2_pcguess (spu_drain.c spu_hop_init: KZ2_SPU_PCGUESS=1 and the 1098 guesses on). The guess is only a hint:
the hop is taken directly only when the register equals it and spu_ib_guess_ok() holds (an enabled pending interrupt
still goes to the drain), else the old path runs. The guess targets join the TU's verified list (spu_ib_guess_register),
like 1098's. In UpdateJob 22 of the 27 unguessed computed hops get a guess (the two `bihz $r17|$r16, $r2` sites at
0xF858/0xF944 jump to the middle of a lifted function, no guess). Host test: tools/spu/test_spu_pcguess.sh (hops on/off
give the same registers and steps; off goes through spu_ib_direct; interrupt pending, wrong target and guesses off
fall back; negative control with the switch ignored; the lifter half on the idiom's real encodings).

